// Normalize  [audioEffect] — bring the loudest sample of a recording to Target. A COLD module: it only
// works on audio already on disk, because the gain depends on the peak and the peak may be the last sample.
// Dropping it in a chain fed by a live input is refused, by name, with what to do instead.
// Its DSP is described in jsdsp.ts beside this file, not compiled into the engine.
cold(true)
plugin({ type: "jsdsp", name: "Normalize" })
params({
  // 1 dB of headroom, the usual answer for a master.
  Target: -1,
  // The measured peak of the input, in dBFS, written by the cold pass. 0 until it has run — which makes
  // the module attenuate rather than boost, the harmless direction to be wrong in.
  Peak: 0,
})
// Peak normalisation. Measures the loudest sample of the whole file and applies the gain that puts it at Target. Only works on a file input: live, there is nothing to measure yet.
